From 20ba59cabb36482cf3e40791617da0946820c282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:32:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: ti: omap: espresso-common: add the bootloader
 reboot modes

The Samsung bootloader of the Galaxy Tab 2 takes its boot mode from the
word at SAR RAM offset 0xff8, and the vendor kernel writes it from a
reboot notifier: 0x1 normal, 0x2 recovery, 0x20 download (Odin) mode.
Without it, "reboot download" can't reach download mode, and a plain
reboot with USB power present comes up through the bootloader's charger
path.

Describe the modes with syscon-reboot-mode on the SAR RAM, and enable
the SAR RAM target module.

The word doubles as mainline's saved L2X0 AUXCTRL value. That is written
once at boot and read back only when resuming from MPUSS OFF, which
doesn't happen after a reboot notifier has run, so the reboot mode can
take it over. The bootloader doesn't need the "RESET" tag the vendor
kernel also writes at 0xff4 (which the kernel's CPU1 low-power code
rewrites anyway).

Tested on a GT-P51xx: download and normal. Recovery is taken from the
vendor kernel and not tested.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi   | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
index 1c10db85788f..5a2656f42fef 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
@@ -751,3 +751,22 @@ bluetooth {
 		interrupt-names = "host-wakeup";
 	};
 };
+
+&sar_target {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&sar_ram {
+	/*
+	 * The Samsung bootloader takes its boot mode from this word. It is
+	 * also the kernel's saved L2X0 AUXCTRL value, which is only read back
+	 * on an MPUSS OFF wakeup, so overwriting it at restart is fine.
+	 */
+	reboot-mode {
+		compatible = "syscon-reboot-mode";
+		offset = <0xff8>;
+		mode-normal = <0x1>;
+		mode-recovery = <0x2>;
+		mode-download = <0x20>;
+	};
+};
